From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:14:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the desktop stays the size of the screen

`0018` made the window the size of the screen and it worked. A tty run
reported a desktop of 2880x1920 -- and 1.37 seconds later, one of 1050x1900.
That is Chromium's default app window on that panel, which is the
`restored_bounds_` `DrmWindowHost::SetFullscreen` records on the way in, and a
window that is not EXACTLY the CRTC's rectangle gets no controller out of
`ScreenManager::FindWindowAt`. So from that moment nothing was drawn at all.

WHAT LEFT FULLSCREEN IS A WATCHDOG ON A WINDOW THAT CANNOT ANSWER IT.
`ExclusiveAccessBubbleViews::Show` arms `presentation_watchdog_timer_` for
1500ms and stops it in `OnFirstPresentation`; on timeout it calls
`ExclusiveAccessManager::ExitExclusiveAccess()`, which for browser-mode
fullscreen is `FullscreenController::ExitFullscreenModeInternal()` and ends in
`BrowserView::ProcessFullscreen(false, ...)` -> `Widget::SetFullscreen(false)`
-> `DrmWindowHost::SetFullscreen(false)` -> `restored_bounds_`. The bubble
exists because `FullscreenController::WindowFullscreenStateChanged` updates it
on the way in, and `GetExclusiveAccessExitBubbleType` answers
`BROWSER_FULLSCREEN_EXIT_INSTRUCTION` for a controller-initiated fullscreen
that is not kiosk -- which is exactly what `--start-fullscreen` is.

And it can never be presented. The bubble is a top-level window of its own:
`SubtleNotificationView::CreatePopupWidget` asks for
`ui::ZOrderLevel::kSecuritySurface`, and `GetNativeWidgetTypeForInitParams`
answers a security surface with `kDesktopNativeWidgetAura` unconditionally, so
that nothing can cover the one piece of UI standing between a page and a
convincing fake desktop. On ozone/drm a second top-level window has no display
controller, `DrmWindow::SchedulePageFlip` takes its `if (!controller_)` branch
and answers `gfx::PresentationFeedback::Failure()`, and a failed presentation
does not run the successful-presentation callbacks -- it keeps them pending
(`cc/trees/presentation_time_callback_buffer.cc`). `OnFirstPresentation` never
runs. The watchdog is not a GPU-hang detector here; it is a 1500ms timer.

The arm above it already says all of this about headless, in the same words,
down to naming `--start-fullscreen` as what it would revert. This is that
arm's twin, and the question is Ozone's rather than the bubble's:
`PlatformRuntimeProperties::presents_every_window` is true by default, because
everywhere a window system puts the pixels on the screen the compositor hands
a frame over and the server is answerable for it. ozone/drm IS the window
system, so it answers false -- in `InitializeUI` rather than beside
`supports_native_pixmaps` in `InitializeGPU`, because the process that has to
know is the browser and out of single-process mode `InitializeGPU` never runs
there. `supports_system_tray_windowing` is the same shape: a platform saying
which windows it cannot host, read from `chrome/` at the one place it decides
something.

NOT KIOSK AND NOT A SWITCH. `IsRunningInAppMode()` would suppress the bubble
and carries the policy surface `0018` refused, and a launcher flag would be a
fact about the ozone platform written down somewhere the ozone platform is
not -- so `--ozone-platform=drm` by hand would bring the timer back. What is
lost is the exit instructions, which on a tty name a chord for a window there
is nothing to exit to; what was lost before was every pixel.

`scripts/test-the-fullscreen-bubble-does-not-undo-fullscreen.sh` reads the
series for both halves: the bubble has to ask and ozone/drm has to answer.
Either alone compiles and does nothing.
